docs/api-reference/analysis/.body:
Brand analysis and audits

The services behind Brand Analysis: the one-line audit and its stages,
the diagnosis, material attached to a new-site audit, content research,
market research, Google Search Console, and fixes proposed to the customer's
own website repository. Package pulse.v1; the least role of each method is
in its table. See Audit a domain.
Notes

Partial results. A diagnosis can return as a partial result: a part that does not finish
is named on the result, and the
rest is returned rather than discarded.
Judged output. Diagnostic.channel_prescriptions and brand_visibility
hold only proposals the plan gate kept;
judgements lists every verdict.
Audit runs. RunAudit keeps running after the call returns, resumes
where it stopped, reuses a recent run unless force is set, and attaches to
a run already in flight. Read the report with GetAuditRun
(AuditRun.score_report).
Progress steps. stage is an informational identifier: show it as-is or map it to your
own labels, but do not rely on the set of steps or their order. A step that
could not run is skipped, with an
error. queue_position is set while a step waits.
The terminal event has an empty stage and the run's final run_status.
Stored reads. The market research List* methods read what earlier
research and audits saved; they search nothing. The service keeps its older
proto name.
Changing a site. ApplyAuditActions (other than plan) and
SiteRepoService.ProposeSiteFix need an admin and the site-change switches
your administrator arms; a proposed fix is a pull request on a new branch.
See Website repository.
Search Console. StartSearchConsoleConnect returns Google's consent
address. When the deployment is not set up for it, the answer says what is
missing. See Google.


