docs/api-reference/leads-and-accounts/.body:
Leads, tenders and accounts

The services behind Leads (people and public tenders), AI calls, agency clients and
Settings › Integrations. Package pulse.v1; the least role of each method
is in its table. See Leads and
Connections.
Notes

Answer vendor pitches. VendorPitchService holds an account's switch (default off), its terms and the partner pipeline. SaveVendorPitch and DecidePartnerPitch need an editor or administrator in their own session (a service account or a loop run is refused); only DecidePartnerPitch can set the stage agreed. GetVendorPitch reports each channel as ready, off or not_available with fixed reason codes, and the last log rows carry codes only, never a sender or a message. See Answer vendor pitches.
Integrations are the caller's own rows, so reading them is open to a
viewer and changing them needs an editor, not an admin. HubSpot and GitHub
connections go through the shared ConnectionsService instead; see
Shared components.
Sign-in connections. StartSocialConnect returns the consent address for
instagram, youtube or linkedin. The answer is configured=false with a
message when the deployment is not set up for that platform.
ListSocialConnections reports one status per platform and, per feature,
the permissions needed and granted. DisconnectSocial revokes the grant at
the platform where its API allows, then deletes the stored tokens. See
Setup.
Outbound. SendOutreachEmail and AICallService.PlaceAICall (the one
RPC that calls a lead) work only when your administrator has armed sending
and calls; a call also needs the lead's recorded consent. See
Switches and arming order.
Agencies. A client is its own owner id. Sending x-pulse-client with a
client the caller is a member of makes that client the caller.
Public tenders (the tender cards on the Leads board) are read from open
procurement data; nothing is sent or submitted. Their service keeps its
older proto name.


