OutreachService
OutreachService — one outreach sequence per lead, from the first touch to a booked meeting (owner, 2026-11-06: "the email automation part managing cold calls until they become meeting prospects"). Cold email, timed follow-ups, CALL tasks for a person (talking points drafted from the lead and the check-up; the call goes through the existing Call command), a LinkedIn touch as a task.
The rules a reader can rely on:  Nothing is sent without approval: every email is a draft until the person approves it (each step, or the rest of the sequence after the first approval, as they chose). Sending is from the person's OWN connected Gmail or Microsoft 365 mailbox and still needs publishing enabled for the deployment and for email.  Every email carries the sender's identity, a postal address and a one-click unsubscribe link, added by PULSE, never by the model; an email missing one is refused by the compliance check.  A sequence stops by itself on a reply, a bounce, an unsubscribe or a booked meeting. An unsubscribe goes on the suppression list and stops every sequence to that address.  Sends keep the per-mailbox daily cap and the lead's working hours (no weekends, no nights). * Only B2B addresses found legitimately (the business's own site or form, the CRM, a published notice) are sequenced.
