OpportunityService — Audience › Opportunities (owner, 2026-10-30): public tenders and private requests for proposals that need what the account sells (websites, custom applications, content …), and a drafted response.
The rules a reader can rely on:  Sources are official open procurement data (EU TED, UK Find a Tender and Contracts Finder, Brazil PNCP, CanadaBuys; US SAM.gov with the account's own key from Integrations) plus private requests for proposals found on public pages. No login is scraped.  Each source reports read (with a count), empty, unreadable (with the reason) or not connected. A source that could not be read is never shown as having nothing.  A figure a notice does not state (value, deadline) is absent, never 0.  Matching is the account's offerings mapped to procurement codes (CPV, UNSPSC, NAICS) plus word matching; every card says why it matched. * A drafted response is a draft: nothing here submits anywhere. The person submits, and records it by moving the card to Submitted.
