AICallService
AICallService places AI voice calls to leads and keeps the records those calls need: the lead's prior express consent, the lead's time zone, the tenant's do-not-call list, each call's outcome and sealed transcript, and the follow-up task a call leaves behind.
PlaceAICall refuses, and returns every reason, unless all hold: - outbound AI calling is enabled for the deployment; - the caller is an editor or admin; - the lead's phone has a consent record (who recorded it, when and how it was given) for THAT number, not revoked: an AI voice is an artificial voice under the TCPA (FCC, February 2024); - the number is not on the tenant's do-not-call list; - the lead's local time (its time zone is required) is inside the account's calling-hours window, itself inside 08:00-21:00; - fewer than max_attempts AI calls to the lead in the last 30 days, and none in progress; - the tenant's caller ID is configured. Every call discloses that it is an AI assistant and who it calls for. Saying "stop" or "do not call" on a call puts the number on the do-not-call list.
Automations call PlaceAICall as a step with origin "automation:" plus the automation id; a refusal is a result (placed=false, refusals), not an RPC error.
