VendorPitchService
ANSWER VENDOR PITCHES (owner request, 2026-11-27). When a vendor or service provider writes to the account trying to sell something similar to, or the same as, what the account sells, PULSE answers with the account's OWN counter-offer: become our client, or partner with us for mutual interest, with our team paid upfront as the account's terms say. A vendor who answers with interest becomes a record in the partner pipeline.
Per-account switch, DEFAULT OFF; on, there is no per-message approval for a confident case (an unsure one waits for a person). Every send still passes the global kill switch, the channel's own switch, My rules and the conscience gate. The terms are the account's own words: PULSE invents no price, term, discount or figure. Moving a record to "agreed" is a person's action only.
