DigitalTwinService
DigitalTwinService — digital twins: a presenter (a name, a role, a language, a voice and, later, a face) for presentations and course materials.
Built in: a small set of personas whose voices are the voices the platform's text-to-speech reports, with their licences. They have no face image yet (a flat colour and initials). When text-to-speech cannot be reached the catalogue says so; nothing is made up.
Your own: the person adds audio and video of THEMSELVES as the base of their digital version. Every sample and every photo or video needs a recorded consent (text version, the statement spoken, when) or it is refused, and the consent can be withdrawn at any time: the media is then deleted. A person sees only their own twins and media (an agency's client is its own owner).
Custom voices and lip-synced video are NOT handled here: Preview of a custom voice says when it is unavailable, presenter videos are PresenterVideoService and a lip-synced one of the person's own face is LipSyncVideoService.
