PresenterVideoService
PresenterVideoService — a presenter video for presentations and course materials (owner, 2026-11-20): a digital twin's appearance image (a built-in persona's card, or the caller's own consented photo or video) beside slides drawn from the script, the twin's voice reading the narration, and the spoken words shown as captions.
What it is, said on every video in its kind: a twin with its own photo or video is a still picture with a voice-over ("presenter video, voice-over"); a built-in persona is a drawn face ("animated presenter (illustration), voice-over"). Neither is lip-synced, and lip_synced is false. A LIP-SYNCED video of the person's own face is made by LipSyncVideoService (lipsync.proto): it replaces the draft's file and the video then says "presenter video, lip-synced (AI-generated)" with lip_synced true.
The caller's own voice or appearance is used only while its consent is active: a twin whose consent was withdrawn is refused, and a video made with it is withdrawn (its file deleted) the next time it is read. Built-in personas need no consent.
A video is made in the background (a later one waits behind the one running). Read it with GetPresenterVideo until state is "ready", then download download_url (signed, expires: read the video again for a fresh one).
Limits, for every video: at most 40 slides, 6 points a slide, 1,500 characters of narration a slide, 2,400 words of narration in all, and 10 minutes (600 seconds) and 100 MB of finished video. Text that does not fit its place is refused with the slide named; it is never cut.
