LipSyncVideoService
LipSyncVideoService makes a lip-synced presenter video of the caller's own twin from a script, using the person's own photo or short video.
A request runs in the background: 1. A voice-over presenter video is made first from the script (playable at once from PresenterVideoService). 2. The lip-synced version follows. It can take minutes for a minute of video; state, progress and an estimate ("about N minutes") are on every read. 3. When it is done the draft's file is replaced by the lip-synced video (the same presenter video id, now kind "presenter video, lip-synced (AI-generated)", lip_synced true). On a failure the draft is left untouched and error_message says why in plain words.
Every lip-synced video carries a visible "AI-generated" label; PULSE v1 offers no way to switch the label off.
Consent: only for the caller's OWN twin whose appearance consent is active. A withdrawn consent refuses the request, cancels a running one and deletes every derived video; deleting the twin does the same. Built-in personas have no real person and are refused here.
The feature can be unavailable; ListLipSyncVideos says so (available, unavailable_reason).
