SelfHealService
Read-only view of the deployment's self-healing monitor, so an operator can see it working. GetStatus is the only RPC; this service observes and never triggers remediation itself.
pulse.v1.SelfHealService, declared in pulse.proto.



Method
Request → Response
Least role
Notes




GetStatus
google.protobuf.Empty → SelfHealStatus
viewer



message SelfHealEvent {
  string type = 1;        // HealthEventType, e.g. "endpoint_unhealthy", "memory_pressure"
  string severity = 2;    // e.g. "warning", "critical"
  string target_id = 3;
  string description = 4;
  bool remediated = 5;    // true if the remediator handled it without error
  google.protobuf.Timestamp at = 6;
}

message SelfHealStatus {
  bool healthy = 1;               // no critical event unresolved in the recent window
  google.protobuf.Timestamp started_at = 2;
  SelfHealEvent last_event = 3;   // unset if nothing has fired yet
  repeated SelfHealEvent recent_events = 4; // most recent first, bounded
  int32 remediation_attempts = 5;
  int32 remediation_failures = 6;
}

OwnerReachService
AGENTS THAT REACH THE USER (owner, 2026-11-20): when PULSE's assistant or an agent cannot answer from the account's own data (the check-up, the leads, the plan have nothing), it may ask the account's OWNER one short question. The question is always in the app (the bell and Settings › Account). It also goes to the owner's own configured WhatsApp or SMS number, but only when the owner opted in here, messaging is configured for the deployment and every safety check passes. The reply (in the app, or by message) is the answer to that one question. Default OFF.
pulse.v1.OwnerReachService, declared in owner_reach.proto.



Method
Request → Response
Least role
Notes




GetOwnerReach
GetOwnerReachRequest → OwnerReach
viewer
The caller's settings, the contacts they can pick, and whether this server can message at all (why not, when it cannot).


SaveOwnerReach
SaveOwnerReachRequest → OwnerReach
editor
Opt in or out, pick the contact and channel, "don't ask me first", quiet hours. Turning the opt-in off at once expires an open message question.


ListOwnerQuestions
ListOwnerQuestionsRequest → ListOwnerQuestionsResponse
viewer
The caller's questions, open first, then newest. Stale ones are expired first.


AnswerOwnerQuestion
